# nr-tui-vm-tools wiring (core): the new crate `mixdog-view-model` (the view model of the terminal UI; this task fills the tool surface, tool work units, tool primitives, tool status and the tool execution contract, and declares the module directories the later vm tasks fill).

The crate is in `native/core/crates/mixdog-view-model` (Cargo.toml, src/{lib,tool_primitives,tool_surface,tool_work_units,tool_status,tool_contract,results,card_model,errors,display}.rs, the stub submodule files under
src/{results,card_model,errors,display}/, tests/tools_twin.rs, tests/recorders/record-tools.mjs, tests/goldens/tools.json). It has no protocol rows, no registration and no SERVICE_PENDING entry: no daemon method uses it yet.
Its consumers are the later view-model tasks (nr-tui-vm-results, nr-tui-vm-errors, nr-tui-vm-display, nr-tui-vm-cards) and the TUI widgets that draw tool cards.

## 1. native/core/Cargo.toml

(a) `[workspace] members`: after `"crates/mixdog-trace",` add

    "crates/mixdog-view-model",

(b) `[workspace.dependencies]`, in the internal crates block after `mixdog-trace = { path = "crates/mixdog-trace" }`:

    mixdog-view-model = { path = "crates/mixdog-view-model" }

No registry crate is added: serde and serde_json are already workspace dependencies. The crate depends on these workspace crates (all downward; nothing depends on `mixdog-view-model` yet): `mixdog-js`,
`mixdog-protocol`, `mixdog-workspace-hack`. `mixdog-termtext` is added to its `[dependencies]` by nr-tui-vm-display (wave 2), not here.

## 2. native/core/Cargo.lock

Add the package entry (cargo writes it; `--locked` needs it present), in name order after `mixdog-trace`:

    [[package]]
    name = "mixdog-view-model"
    version = "1.5.0"
    dependencies = [
     "mixdog-js",
     "mixdog-protocol",
     "mixdog-workspace-hack",
     "serde",
     "serde_json",
    ]

## 3. native/core/crates/mixdog-workspace-hack/Cargo.toml

Run `cargo hakari generate` (the new crate adds no registry crate, so the file is expected not to change; `cargo hakari verify` is the check).

## 4. The recording

`tests/goldens/tools.json` is written by `node native/core/crates/mixdog-view-model/tests/recorders/record-tools.mjs --tree <the Node tree> --fixtures <native/core/fixtures>` and checked with the same command plus
`--check native/core/crates/mixdog-view-model/tests/goldens/tools.json`. It was recorded here from `packages/protocol-client/src/rows/` and `src/runtime/shared/tool-execution-contract.mjs` of this tree (the recorder reads
`src/runtime/shared/` first and falls back to the rows copies; `tool-surface.mjs` and `tool-work-units.mjs` exist only as the rows copies in this tree). tests/tools_twin.rs reads the file and needs no fixture directory.
Two recorded outputs are Node exceptions (`code_graph` with a null argument, `classifyToolCategory` and `aggregateToolCategoryEntries` read `args.mode` of null); the twin skips them.

## 5. Nothing else

No `compose_flip.rs` change (no protocol method), no `pending-rows`.
